Ported/adapted files include the computer-use host, lease/provider contracts,
macOS Cua provider, Windows UIA provider, native Swift helper, cursor asset,
and build-time Cua source patches. The Windows helper was extracted from
windows-uia-script.ts; its scroll amount handling was corrected. The Go port
adds cancellation, serialized execution, bounded snapshot storage, strict
argument validation, Eino multimodal output and a legacy text adapter.
Native build verification added macOS 14 SDK concurrency annotation fixes,
PID-based actor-boundary handling for focus restoration, Swift 6.2 dependency
preflight checks, and frozen dependency resolution.

The public Config / Param / Tool / Execute / Cleanup API is inspired by
CloudWeGo Eino-ext's BrowserUse tool (Copyright 2025 CloudWeGo Authors,
Apache-2.0):
https://github.com/cloudwego/eino-ext/tree/main/components/tool/browseruse

The Swift helper resolves trycua/cua and the MCP Swift SDK via Swift Package
Manager. Their respective licenses and notices apply to those dependencies;
no prebuilt dependency or helper executable is included in this source tree.
